#![TODO]
//! Known WIR miscompile (issue #1415): an imported (non-entry) module that
//! returns a cross-module struct (here an imported Gale parser's `CstNode`) *by
//! value* and then borrows + recurses on it has the binding's local lowered as
//! `i32` instead of a GC ref, producing invalid core Wasm
//! ("expected i32, found (ref $type)").
//!
//! Root cause: `Elaborator::lookup_function_return_type` returns a pre-resolved
//! `TypeId` for entry-point callees but re-resolves the return-type AST for
//! callees in imported modules; that re-resolution yields a non-canonical
//! `TypeId` for the cross-module struct. Drop `#![TODO]` once fixed — the test
//! should then pass and the runner reports it as resolved.
//!
//! See package-gale/example/eval.wado for the safe form (recurse on the
//! loop-bound child instead of returning a `CstNode` by value).

use { depth } from "./sub/wir_xmodule_return_eval.wado";

test "nested parens give nesting depth" {
    assert depth(&"1") == 1;
    assert depth(&"(1)") == 2;
    assert depth(&"((1))") == 3;
}

__DATA__
{"test": {}}
